# Task153 `kda_prologue`, write-side projection.
#
# The hand-written kernel of 153 reads four program-uniform scalars per program
# (`chunk_indices[c,0]`, `cu_seqlens[seq]`, ...) and then writes contiguous runs at
# `base + arange(lane)`. This program expresses exactly that write shape with the
# staged `store_at` primitive: one block write per program, its base read once from
# a 1-D int32 device table.
#
# `store_at` is NOT registered in compiler/frontend/operator.py yet: that registry
# is being merged by the segmented_cumsum work, and these two operators are added in
# one coordinated commit. The lowering is exercised by test/test_store_at.py.
#
# Layout note (the observed 153 shapes): `hb == hv` because `hv * kdim <= 2048`, so
# each chunk writes BT full token rows = BT*HV*K contiguous elements, and the chunks
# tile T. That is one contiguous run per chunk, i.e. exactly this operator's shape.
pipeline kda_prologue_store {
    input dst    : bf16[T]
    input starts : int32[C]
    input values : bf16[C,BT,K]
    out = store_at(dst, starts, values)
    output out
}
